{#
/**
 * @file
 * Flow diagram of the homepage decision; the path this search took is lit.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - query: the search text.
 * - path: 'urgent', 'ask' or 'hybrid'.
 * - images: public path of the module's images directory (trailing slash).
 */
#}
<p class="med-flow__intro">{% trans %}Every homepage search goes through two checks, in this order. Your search, <strong>“{{ query }}”</strong>, took the <span class="med-flow__you">highlighted</span> path.{% endtrans %}</p>
<ol class="med-flow" role="list">
  <li class="med-flow__node med-flow__node--input is-taken">{{ 'Your words'|t }}</li>
  <li class="med-flow__step{{ path == 'urgent' ? ' is-taken' }}">
    <div class="med-flow__check is-taken">
      <span class="med-flow__q">{{ '1. Urgent wording? (an emergency or a crisis)'|t }}</span>
      <span class="med-flow__how">{{ 'fixed phrases such as “chest pain”, “can’t breathe”, “throat swelling”, “passed out”, stroke signs, “overdose” or self-harm words'|t }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="med-flow__branch{{ path == 'urgent' ? ' is-taken' }}"><span class="med-flow__yes">{{ 'yes'|t }}</span>
      <div class="med-flow__node med-flow__node--urgent">
        <strong class="med-flow__title"><img src="{{ images }}urgent.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> {{ 'Safety message'|t }}</strong>
        <span>{{ '“Call 911 now” (or 988 for a crisis). Shown first, instead of search results or an AI answer.'|t }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="med-flow__no{{ path != 'urgent' ? ' is-taken' }}">{{ 'no'|t }}</li>
  <li class="med-flow__step{{ path == 'ask' ? ' is-taken' }}">
    <div class="med-flow__check{{ path != 'urgent' ? ' is-taken' }}">
      <span class="med-flow__q">{{ '2. A question?'|t }}</span>
      <span class="med-flow__how">{{ 'ends with “?”, or starts with what / why / how…, or “is the”, “can I”, “do you”…'|t }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="med-flow__branch{{ path == 'ask' ? ' is-taken' }}"><span class="med-flow__yes">{{ 'yes'|t }}</span>
      <div class="med-flow__node med-flow__node--ask">
        <strong class="med-flow__title"><img src="{{ images }}rag.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> {{ 'Ask (RAG)'|t }}</strong>
        <ol class="med-flow__pipe">
          <li><img src="{{ images }}postgresql.svg" alt="" width="18" height="18"> {{ 'Semantic search (pgvector) picks the 3 closest topics'|t }}</li>
          <li><span class="med-flow__ai" aria-hidden="true">✦</span> {{ 'Ollama writes an answer from those topics only'|t }}</li>
          <li><span class="med-flow__ai" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> {{ 'Every sentence must cite a source, or it is dropped'|t }}</li>
        </ol>
        <span class="med-flow__out">{{ '→ a short answer with citations'|t }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="med-flow__no{{ path == 'hybrid' ? ' is-taken' }}">{{ 'no'|t }}</li>
  <li class="med-flow__node med-flow__node--hybrid{{ path == 'hybrid' ? ' is-taken' }}">
    <strong class="med-flow__title"><img src="{{ images }}solr.png" alt="" width="20" height="20"><img src="{{ images }}postgresql.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> {{ 'Hybrid (Keyword + Semantic)'|t }}</strong>
    <div class="med-flow__lists">
      <span><img src="{{ images }}solr.png" alt="" width="18" height="18"> {{ 'Keyword list (Apache Solr)'|t }}</span>
      <span class="med-flow__plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      <span><img src="{{ images }}postgresql.svg" alt="" width="18" height="18"> {{ 'Semantic list (pgvector)'|t }}</span>
    </div>
    <span class="med-flow__merge">{{ '↓ merged by RRF (k = 60): topics high in both lists rise to the top'|t }}</span>
    <span class="med-flow__out">{{ '→ a ranked list of health topics'|t }}</span>
  </li>
</ol>
<p class="med-flow__note">{% trans %}<strong>Good to know:</strong> check 2 is a simple word pattern, not AI, so it is instant and predictable. It misses some questions: “what’s HbA1c”, “explain HbA1c” and “should a diabetic eat rice” currently go to Hybrid. RRF never decides the path; it only orders Hybrid’s topics.{% endtrans %}</p>
